# Environment variables

## Files

- **Secrets / local values:** `.env.local` (gitignored)—never commit
- **Documented names:** always maintain `.env.example` (no real secrets)
- Parse only via `src/lib/env.ts` with Zod (**validation** skill)

## One name only

- One canonical name per setting; no `process.env.A || process.env.B`
- Never prefix secrets with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`; never import server env from `"use client"`

## `.env.example` style

- Short and scannable: `NAME=` plus optional placeholder
- Comments only to **group** related vars (e.g. `# Auth`, `# Supabase`)—not feature essays
- Fail fast on missing required keys; errors name the exact variable

## Promote environments

Order: **local → staging → production**.

- Small/sure work may skip local and land on **staging** first
- **Never** skip straight to **production**
- Tell the user exact name, where to set it (`.env.local` / host staging / host production), and server vs `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
